// corner.rule -- SYNTHETIC regression guard for the §4.05 corner-to-corner fix.
// Two axis-aligned squares placed DIAGONALLY corner-to-corner (nearest vertices
// 0.212um apart) plus a FACING pair (0.15um). NO vendor data.
//
// CORNER.PLAIN.EUCLID: a plain Euclidian REGION spacing rule. Euclidian metric
//   "also considers the corners", so the 0.212um<0.23 diagonal gap is a REAL
//   violation and MUST be flagged. This is the leniency-mask regression guard:
//   the ABUT-gated corner drop must NEVER suppress a plain-Euclidian corner
//   violation (a false-clean is worse than a false-fail). -> 3 (2 diagonal + 1 facing).
// CORNER.ABUT: the same check WITH an ABUT qualifier (abutting-layer corner
//   handling). The diagonal abutment corner is dropped; only the facing pair
//   (projection>0) survives. -> 1.
LAYER met 20 0

CORNER.PLAIN.EUCLID {
  EXTERNAL met < 0.23 REGION
}

CORNER.ABUT {
  EXTERNAL met < 0.23 ABUT < 90 REGION
}
